#sleela 1.6
//
// Moria — the Title Bar logo
// ==========================
// A thin, non-interactive SleelaUI widget that paints a REAL image file (the
// trimmed, transparent-background D&D mark) as the Moria window's title logo.
//
// It mirrors the vendored SLImage widget's shape exactly — an SLWidget whose
// constructor bottoms out in a `ui*` SLVM bridge built-in — but loads an image
// *from a path* (`uiImageFile`, SleelaUI C ABI slui_image_file()) rather than
// drawing a centred glyph tile. The toolkit draws it with its natural alpha, so
// the cleared (transparent) background lets the slick-black stone show through
// and only the red mark reads.
//
// The vendored toolkit at ../../1/sources/user-interface is kept byte-for-byte
// with upstream mearvk/SLeeLa, so this presentation-only helper lives in the
// Moria tree beside MoriaUI rather than inside the shared widget vocabulary.
//
// Headless / no-loader fallback: callers check loaded(); when the image cannot
// be bound (no display, missing file, or a build without the uiImageFile
// bridge) they fall back to the text heading, so the title always reads.
//
class MoriaTitleLogo extends SLWidget {

    // The logo asset, relative to the Moria module root (ui-sleela runs from
    // moria/, matching how MoriaUI resolves its sibling game/ sources).
    static String ASSET = "images/D&D-logo-title.png";

    // Create the title logo inside `parent`, drawn no taller than `maxHeight`
    // px (width scales to preserve the mark's aspect; "careful, adult size").
    // Returns true when a real image widget was bound, false when the caller
    // should fall back to the text title.
    boolean createIn(SLWidget parent, int maxHeight) {
        widget = uiImageFile(parent.handle(), ASSET, 0, maxHeight);
        if (widget >= 0) {
            // Centre the mark in the title area and let it breathe a little.
            setAlign(SLWidget.ALIGN_CENTER, SLWidget.ALIGN_CENTER);
            setMargin(4, 0, 4, 0);
        }
        return loaded();
    }

    boolean loaded() { return widget >= 0; }
}
